{
  "title": "ecs-dynamodb-rps-ceiling \u2014 attribution",
  "description": "Live attribution dashboard: which resource is the RPS ceiling during a k6 run \u2014 DynamoDB, the ECS task, or the edge. Read top-to-bottom while a run is in flight.",
  "tags": [
    "ecs-dynamodb-rps-ceiling"
  ],
  "timezone": "utc",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "10s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-1h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "table_name",
        "type": "textbox",
        "label": "DynamoDB table",
        "description": "Table name used in every DynamoDB CloudWatch dimension on this dashboard.",
        "query": "ecs-dynamodb-rps-ceiling",
        "current": {
          "text": "ecs-dynamodb-rps-ceiling",
          "value": "ecs-dynamodb-rps-ceiling"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "1. Attribution \u2014 which resource is the ceiling?",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "DynamoDB ThrottledRequests (headline)",
      "description": "The whole decision in one line: zero = DynamoDB is not the ceiling, non-zero = it is. This is the total across read+write throttling; if it climbs while the service is still hitting its SLI, the ceiling is the database, not the app or the ALB.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "cloudwatch",
        "uid": "a4139e7c-dc84-47c8-b90b-d710ec0fe3fb"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "cloudwatch",
            "uid": "a4139e7c-dc84-47c8-b90b-d710ec0fe3fb"
          },
          "namespace": "AWS/DynamoDB",
          "metricName": "ThrottledRequests",
          "statistic": "Sum",
          "dimensions": {
            "TableName": "$table_name"
          },
          "region": "eu-central-1",
          "period": "60",
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0,
          "matchExact": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "spanNulls": true
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Read vs write throttling",
      "description": "Splits the headline ThrottledRequests by side. ReadThrottleEvents currently reads zero because reads have not throttled yet in any run so far \u2014 keep the panel, it will populate once reads saturate. WriteThrottleEvents rising alone points at write capacity/WCU specifically, not the table as a whole.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "cloudwatch",
        "uid": "a4139e7c-dc84-47c8-b90b-d710ec0fe3fb"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "cloudwatch",
            "uid": "a4139e7c-dc84-47c8-b90b-d710ec0fe3fb"
          },
          "namespace": "AWS/DynamoDB",
          "metricName": "ReadThrottleEvents",
          "statistic": "Sum",
          "dimensions": {
            "TableName": "$table_name"
          },
          "region": "eu-central-1",
          "period": "60",
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0,
          "matchExact": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "cloudwatch",
            "uid": "a4139e7c-dc84-47c8-b90b-d710ec0fe3fb"
          },
          "namespace": "AWS/DynamoDB",
          "metricName": "WriteThrottleEvents",
          "statistic": "Sum",
          "dimensions": {
            "TableName": "$table_name"
          },
          "region": "eu-central-1",
          "period": "60",
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0,
          "matchExact": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "spanNulls": true
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "2. DynamoDB server-side latency (the uncontaminated clock)",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "SuccessfulRequestLatency by operation (Average & Maximum)",
      "description": "The DynamoDB-reported clock, split by GetItem/PutItem/Query. This is what db_wall_avg_by_route is compared against \u2014 that metric is wall-clock around the SDK await and absorbs event-loop queueing (measured 12.1x inflation with the database unchanged), so a gap between this panel and it is the queueing signal, not extra DB time. Read that gap PER ROUTE: each route is compared against the sum of only the operations it issues (/reports issues Query then PutItem), which is what the \"Queueing delay by route\" panel computes. db_ms was the k6 Trend that carried this number before the SLI moved into the service; it no longer exists. Average and Maximum both shown: Maximum surfaces tail spikes Average hides.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "cloudwatch",
        "uid": "a4139e7c-dc84-47c8-b90b-d710ec0fe3fb"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "cloudwatch",
            "uid": "a4139e7c-dc84-47c8-b90b-d710ec0fe3fb"
          },
          "namespace": "AWS/DynamoDB",
          "metricName": "SuccessfulRequestLatency",
          "statistic": "Average",
          "dimensions": {
            "TableName": "$table_name",
            "Operation": [
              "GetItem",
              "PutItem",
              "Query"
            ]
          },
          "region": "eu-central-1",
          "period": "60",
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0,
          "matchExact": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "cloudwatch",
            "uid": "a4139e7c-dc84-47c8-b90b-d710ec0fe3fb"
          },
          "namespace": "AWS/DynamoDB",
          "metricName": "SuccessfulRequestLatency",
          "statistic": "Maximum",
          "dimensions": {
            "TableName": "$table_name",
            "Operation": [
              "GetItem",
              "PutItem",
              "Query"
            ]
          },
          "region": "eu-central-1",
          "period": "60",
          "metricQueryType": 0,
          "metricEditorMode": 0,
          "matchExact": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "unit": "ms"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "3. Capacity headroom (saturation as convergence, not a number)",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 19
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Read capacity: consumed vs provisioned",
      "description": "Consumed*CapacityUnits is a Sum-per-period metric (units used in the preceding 60s); Provisioned*CapacityUnits is already expressed as units/second. To compare them as rates, divide the consumed line by 60 (the period below) \u2014 this panel shows the raw values, not pre-divided. Consumed converging on or crossing provisioned is read capacity becoming the ceiling, and should line up with ReadThrottleEvents in row 1.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "cloudwatch",
        "uid": "a4139e7c-dc84-47c8-b90b-d710ec0fe3fb"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 20
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
