    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "7. Attribution — the four discriminators",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 55
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "DB wall-clock vs DynamoDB's own clock",
      "description": "db_wall_avg_by_route is wall-clock time around the SDK await, which absorbs event-loop queueing (measured 12.1x inflation with the database unchanged). cloudwatch_srl_by_operation is DynamoDB's own reported clock, scraped by the collector. The gap between the two lines is the queueing signal, not extra DB time — compare against the \"Queueing delay by route\" panel.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 56
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
          },
          "expr": ${jsonencode(db_wall_avg_by_route)}
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
          },
          "expr": ${jsonencode(cloudwatch_srl_by_operation)}
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "unit": "ms"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Queueing delay by route",
      "description": "db_wall_avg_by_route minus DynamoDB's own reported clock for the operations THAT route issues (slo.yaml attribution.operations: /items/:pk/:sk → GetItem, /items → PutItem, /feeds/:pk → Query, /reports → Query + PutItem). Not a table-wide average — averaging unlike operations together, BatchWriteItem from seeding included, subtracted ~1.8 ms too little from /reports. Positive and growing ⇒ service-bound (event-loop queueing), not DB-bound. Shows NaN for any route with no traffic in the window — it is a 0/0 average, not a broken panel. At idle, most routes read NaN because the heartbeat touches each route only once a minute; the value resolves once real load is running.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 56
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
          },
          "expr": ${jsonencode(queueing_ms_by_route)}
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "unit": "ms"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 23,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "CPU saturation",
      "description": "CPU seconds burned per second (by task), over the 0.25 vCPU Fargate ceiling. 1.0 is the ceiling — a task pinned at or above it is CPU-bound regardless of what the DB clock says. READ IT ONE WAY ONLY: that is sufficient evidence of CPU-bound, never necessary. http.server.cpu.duration sums only the two bracketed synchronous blocks in src/handlers.js (feed's summarize, report's pbkdf2); JSON serialisation, AWS SDK work and the OTel export are uncounted, and getItem/putItem bracket nothing so they contribute no series at all. A task can be genuinely pinned while this panel reads 0.2 — when it is low but event-loop utilisation is near 1, the CPU is unaccounted, not absent (spec section 5).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 56
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
          },
          "expr": ${jsonencode(cpu_saturation_ratio)}
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "spanNulls": true
          },
          "unit": "percentunit"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 24,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Event-loop delay p99 by task",
      "description": "nodejs_eventloop_delay_p99_seconds, by (instance) — one line per task; four lines once Task 20 brings autoscaling to 4 tasks. A rising delay here, with CPU saturation flat, points at blocking work off the CPU-accounting path rather than raw compute.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
